  "facade": "e5 = north face on the forecourt, u from the east end (114.3,-90.4). 33 (crop): 2 storeys + hipped red-tile roof, eaves ~9 m (wall ~290 px at ~31 px/m), seven round-arched upper windows (u 1.9-16.3 on the scale given by the roof ends) and an arched vehicle gate; the photo puts the gate at u ~14, OSM gate node 9937882129 / service tunnel 1085709199 at u ~11.7 (R16): u 13.0 used. The west third is hidden by a cypress in 33: two more upper windows there (u 18.8, 21.4) and two ground windows are assumed.",
  "e4": "east face on the narrow stretch (y -90..-106): not in any photo (behind the cameras of 13/21); given the police row's tall round-arched windows with dark louvred shutters (05, 21) on both storeys."
